  },
  "articleBody": "When your door isn't quite right, it's often a puzzle to figure out if it's a hinge problem, a latch issue, or something else entirely. Let's break it down. If your door sags or rubs along the top or bottom of the frame, chances are it's a hinge problem. Loose or worn-out hinges can cause the door to drop, leading to friction. Try tightening the screws first; if that doesn't work, the hinges themselves might need replacing or the door might need rehanging. On the other hand, if the door closes fine but won't stay latched, or you have to really yank on the handle, the issue is likely with the latch or the strike plate. The strike plate might be misaligned, or the latch mechanism itself could be faulty. Sometimes, simply adjusting the strike plate can solve the problem. HH Remodeling LLC has plenty of experience diagnosing these tricky door issues and can quickly determine the best course of action, whether it's a simple adjustment or a more involved repair. Let us take a look and get your door working perfectly.",
